==Polish==
{{wp|lang=pl}}

===Etymology===
Considered derogatory until the 19th century; now the standard, neutral word. Origin {{unc|pl|nocap=1}}; probably either from {{inh|pl|zlw-opl|kob|t=pigpen}} or {{m|zlw-opl|koba|t=mare}} (the suffix {{m|pl||-ieta}} is found in some contemporaneous female names ({{m|pl|Markieta}}, {{m|pl|Elżbieta}}, {{m|pl|Greta}})) or may derive from {{inh|pl|sla-pro|*kobь}}, from {{inh|pl|ine-pro|*kob-}}. {{displaced|pl|niewiasta}} (now considered poetic) and {{m|pl|żona}} (meaning narrowed down to "wife").

